---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL } from '../lib/site.js';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Terms of Service', url: '/terms/' },
];
const host = SITE.domain.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms governing your use of GarageDoorHQ — our content, directory listings, cost estimates, licence verification and limitation of liability."
  canonical="/terms/"
>
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />

    <article style="margin-top:1rem;">
      <h1 style="margin:1rem 0 .5rem;">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:0 0 2rem;font-size:.85rem;">
        Last updated: {LEGAL.lastUpdated}
      </p>

      <div class="prose">
        <h2>About these terms</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are a contract between you and <strong>{LEGAL.legalName}</strong>,
          {LEGAL.address} ("we", "us"), and govern your use of {host} (the "Service").
          By using the Service you accept these terms. If you do not accept them, please
          do not use the Service.
        </p>

        <h2>Your use of our content</h2>
        <p>
          The content on this website was created, compiled, prepared, selected and
          arranged by us, using our own methods and judgment and through the expenditure
          of substantial time and effort. The Service and its content are proprietary and
          protected by these terms, copyright law and other intellectual property laws,
          including as a collective work or compilation. We provide it for your personal,
          non-commercial use.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may not use, or authorise a third party to use, the Service or its content
          in any manner that (i) is a source of or substitute for the Service or its
          content; (ii) affects our ability to earn money in connection with the Service;
          or (iii) competes with the Service. These restrictions apply to any robot,
          spider, scraper, crawler or other automated means, and to any similar manual
          process. You agree not to bypass any robot exclusion headers or other measures
          limiting automated access.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may quote short extracts for comment, review or news reporting, provided you
          credit {SITE.name} and link to the page you took them from.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>One exception, and it is deliberate.</strong> Business listing data on
          this site derives from Foursquare Open Source Places, distributed by the Overture
          Maps Foundation under the Apache License 2.0. That underlying data remains
          available to you under its own licence directly from its source, and nothing in
          these terms purports to restrict your rights in it. What we claim is our
          selection, filtering, verification, arrangement and written content — not the
          openly licensed facts themselves.
        </p>

        <h2>Cost guides are estimates, not professional advice</h2>
        <p>
          Our guides publish typical price ranges and averages for garage door work. These
          are general information drawn from market research. They are <strong>not</strong>
          {' '}a quote, an appraisal, or professional engineering, financial, legal or tax
          advice, and they do not account for your specific door, opening, opener or local
          market.
        </p>
        <p>
          Prices change and vary considerably by region, season, door size and installer.
          Always obtain written quotes before making a decision, and rely on the
          contractor's assessment rather than ours.
        </p>

        <h2>Safety content</h2>
        <p>
          Some of our content describes work that is dangerous, in particular anything
          involving garage door springs and cables, which hold substantial stored energy.
          Where we advise against a task, that advice is deliberate and we do not publish
          instructions for it. Nothing on this Service is a substitute for a qualified
          technician, and any work you choose to attempt is at your own risk.
        </p>

        <h2>Directory listings</h2>
        <p>
          Our directory includes garage door business information compiled from openly
          licensed and publicly available business data. We are not affiliated with, and
          do not endorse, recommend, certify, vet or guarantee any listed business. A
          listing is not a recommendation, and we do not rank businesses by quality. No
          business pays for inclusion, position or prominence.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What licence verification does and does not mean.</strong> In California,
          Florida and Arizona — the only states that license garage door work as a distinct
          trade — a listing may show a verified licence badge. That badge means one
          specific thing: we matched a licence number to a record on that state's public
          register at the date shown. It does <strong>not</strong> mean we have verified
          insurance, workmanship, pricing, qualifications, or that the licence remains
          current now. We do not inspect work and we do not visit businesses. Everywhere
          else, no licence is checked because there is no garage-door-specific state
          register to check against, and those pages say so.
        </p>
        <p>
          Listings are provided for information only. Any dealings you have with a listed
          business — including any contract, payment or dispute — are solely between you
          and that business. We are not a party to them and accept no responsibility for
          them. We recommend you verify licensing and insurance independently before
          hiring anyone.
        </p>
        <p>
          Information may be incomplete, out of date or inaccurate. If you own a listed
          business and want your entry corrected or removed, email
          {' '}<a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.contactEmail}`}>{LEGAL.contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Submitting a listing</h2>
        <p>
          If you submit your business to us, you confirm you are authorised to do so and
          that the information you give is accurate. We may publish, decline, edit or
          remove any submission at our discretion, and we do not guarantee that a
          submitted business will be listed or remain listed. We do not charge for
          listing, and paying us is not an option we offer.
        </p>

        <h2>Advertising and commercial relationships</h2>
        <p>
          We may display advertising served by third-party advertising networks and
          technology providers, and by media agencies, exchanges and their partners acting
          for advertisers. We may also participate in affiliate or referral arrangements
          under which we earn a commission.
        </p>
        <p>
          Advertising is selected by those third parties and its presence is not an
          endorsement by us. Advertising never affects which businesses are listed or in
          what order. Where we have a commercial relationship that could reasonably affect
          how you read our content, we will disclose it. How advertising affects your data
          is explained in our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-party links and content</h2>
        <p>
          The Service links to third-party websites, including state licensing registers,
          and embeds third-party content such as maps. We do not control those sites and
          are not responsible for their content, accuracy or privacy practices. Following
          an external link is at your own risk.
        </p>

        <h2>Availability</h2>
        <p>
          We provide the Service "as is" and "as available". We do not guarantee it will be
          uninterrupted, error-free or continuously available, and we may change, suspend
          or discontinue any part of it at any time without notice.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, we exclude all warranties, express or
          implied, as to the accuracy, completeness or fitness for purpose of the Service
          and its content. We are not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use
          of, or reliance on, the Service — including any decision to repair or replace a
          garage door or opener, any dealings with a listed business, any reliance on a
          licence check, or any costs that differ from our published estimates.
        </p>
        <p>
          Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability where it would be unlawful to
          do so, including for death or personal injury caused by negligence, or for fraud.
          Some jurisdictions do not allow certain exclusions, so parts of this section may
          not apply to you.
        </p>

        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains what data we collect, the
          cookies we set and your rights over that data. It forms part of these terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms from time to time. The current version is always the
          one on this page, with the date shown above. Continuing to use the Service after
          a change means you accept the updated terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of {LEGAL.governingLaw}, and the courts of
          {' '}{LEGAL.governingLaw} have jurisdiction over any dispute. If you are a
          consumer, this does not deprive you of the protection of any mandatory consumer
          rights available under the law of the country where you live.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms:
          {' '}<a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.contactEmail}`}>{LEGAL.contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
